course: dictionary
lesson: 97
title: Words that carry a heavy meaning
level: primary-6
stars: 0
explain: Some words describe a serious problem, and «addiction» is one of them. Context helps you see its meaning: «Alcoholism, or alcohol addiction, is an illness in which a person needs alcohol so badly they cannot stop even when it hurts them and their family.» The clues are «cannot stop» and «hurts them», so addiction means a strong need that is hard to control, even when it causes harm.
explain: Check your meaning by swapping it into the sentence. Try "a strong need that is hard to stop" in place of addiction, and the sentence still makes sense. That tells you your meaning is right.
explain: Writers also use the word in a lighter way. Someone might say «my chocolate addiction» to mean they really love chocolate. The word «my» and the joking tone are the clues. This is informal, so it does not mean a real illness.
fact: Addiction is a noun. Its plural is addictions.
fact: «Addiction» means a strong need to keep doing or taking something, even when it causes harm.
fact: Things that can cause addiction include nicotine, alcohol, some drugs, gambling, and sometimes screens and games.
fact: «Recovery» means getting better after an addiction and staying off it.
fact: Phrases to know: addiction to, overcome an addiction, screen addiction.
exercise: «Alcoholism, or alcohol addiction, is an illness in which a person needs alcohol so badly they cannot stop.» What does addiction mean here? | *A strong need that is hard to stop, even when it causes harm | A rule about when to go to bed | A small, sweet snack eaten at break | A hobby that people share with friends
exercise: Ruby says, «my chocolate addiction», and she is joking. What does addiction mean in her words? | *A very strong liking for something | A recipe for making cake | A serious illness that needs a doctor | A warning sign on a packet
exercise: «Gambling addiction means a person keeps betting to win back losses.» Which action is a sign of gambling addiction? | Playing a board game with a friend | Saving coins in a jar each week | *Betting again to win back money already lost | Opening a savings account at the bank
test: «In recovery» means recovering from an addiction and staying off it. What does recovering mean? | Forgetting all about it | Going on a holiday | *Getting better and staying off it | Getting a new job
test: «Went into treatment» means a person went to a clinic to get help with an addiction. Where did the person go? | A school | *A clinic | A park | A supermarket
exam: Which phrase best describes someone who cannot stop using their phone, even when it harms their sleep and homework? | sunny day | *screen addiction | birthday party | pencil case
